<title>BELGIUM: ECOFIN discusses draft energy tax.</title>
<headline>ECOFIN discusses draft energy tax.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The ECOFIN Council held preparatory discussions on Monday on a new proposal to raise and extend minimum taxes on energy, but a political debate on the controversial issue must still take place, Dutch finance minister Gerrit Zalm told a press conference.</p>
<p>&quot;We've provided a method of working which maximises chances of progress in this area,&quot; Zalm said.</p>
<p>The Commission has proposed raising minimum excise duties on motor fuel and to extend the duties to electricity, coal and natural gas.</p>
<p>Britain has said it will oppose the plan, which requires unanimous approval. Portugal, Spain, Ireland and Greece have also voiced reservations, a diplomat said.</p>
</text>
